.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt SHA256SUM 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sha256sum
.Nd compute or check SHA-256 file digests
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm
.Fl c Ar list
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Print a lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 digest, two spaces, and a file name
for each input.
No operands reads standard input, labelled
.Ql - ;
an explicit
.Ql -
also reads standard input.
.Pp
.Fl c Ar list
reads a UTF-8 list file.
Each nonempty line must contain a 64-character expected digest, two spaces,
and the exact file name.
The expected digest is compared without letter case.
Relative names resolve from the working directory, not the list's directory.
Print
.Ql name: OK
or
.Ql name: FAILED ;
continue after malformed lines, mismatches and unreadable files.
An empty list succeeds without checking anything.
GNU binary-marker and escaped-name list forms are not implemented.
.Pp
Only a first
.Fl c
selects check mode and requires exactly one list operand.
Other dash-leading arguments except
.Ql -
are usage errors; there is no
.Ql --
terminator.
The command reads visible files, never changes them, and provides byte
consistency rather than proof of origin.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after successful hashing, or when all nonempty list entries match;
1 for a mismatch, malformed list or input error; 2 for usage.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sha256sum /home/operator/document
sha256sum -c /home/operator/SHA256SUMS
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
